1. Added proper TRPC client setup using `createClient` and `httpBatchLink`
2. Added QueryClientProvider from @tanstack/react-query
3. Created proper instances of QueryClient and TRPC client using useState to maintain stability
4. Wrapped the component in a Suspense boundary to handle loading states
5. Removed the manual mock of TRPC and instead used the proper client setup
6. Properly structured the providers to ensure all required context is available

This should resolve the "Failed to fetch dynamically imported module" error by providing the proper context and setup for the TRPC provider. The component should now be able to render properly with all the necessary providers in place.

